    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Les métiers",
     "md": "- a **teacher** (enseignant), a **farmer** (agriculteur), a **nurse** (infirmier), a **doctor** (médecin), a **driver** (chauffeur), a **mechanic** (mécanicien), a **tailor** (couturier), a **trader** (commerçant).\n- On dit : « She is **a** nurse. » (article a / an obligatoire).\n- Question : What does your father do ? / What is your father ?"
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Les directions",
     "md": "- Where is the bank ? — It is **opposite** the market / **next to** the post office / **behind** the school.\n- **Go straight on**, **turn left**, **turn right**, **at the crossroads**."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : métier",
     "statement": "Complète : My mother takes care of sick people. She is a ____.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Elle soigne les malades : nurse (ou doctor)."
      },
      {
       "md": "On relit la phrase obtenue pour vérifier la forme du verbe et le sens."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**nurse**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : direction",
     "statement": "Tu es à l'école. Indique le chemin de la banque : tout droit, puis à gauche.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Utilise Go straight on puis turn left."
      },
      {
       "md": "On relit la phrase obtenue pour vérifier la forme du verbe et le sens."
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Go straight on, then turn left. The bank is on your right.**"
    },
